{
  "id": "validate-binary-search-tree",
  "title": "Validate Binary Search Tree",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "categories": ["tree", "dfs"],
  "descriptionMd": "Given the `root` of a binary tree, decide whether it is a **valid binary search tree**.\n\nA tree qualifies when, for every node:\n- every value in its left subtree is **strictly less** than the node's value,\n- every value in its right subtree is **strictly greater** than the node's value,\n- and both subtrees are themselves valid binary search trees.\n\n**Example 1**\n\n```\nroot = [2, 1, 3]\n→ true\n```\n\n**Example 2**\n\n```\nroot = [5, 1, 4, null, null, 3, 6]\n→ false\n```\nThe root is 5, but its right child is 4, which is smaller.\n\n**Example 3**\n\n```\nroot = [5, 4, 6, null, null, 3, 7]\n→ false\n```\nEach node beats its direct children, yet 3 sits in the right subtree of 5.",
  "constraints": ["1 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 10⁴", "-2³¹ ≤ Node.val ≤ 2³¹ - 1"],
  "hints": ["Comparing a node only with its immediate children is not enough.", "As you descend, every node inherits a range of values it is allowed to take. How does that range change when you go left or right?", "Equal values are not allowed anywhere in the tree."],
  "signature": {
    "functionName": "isValidBST",
    "params": [{ "name": "root", "type": "TreeNode" }],
    "returns": "bool"
  },
  "comparator": "exact",
  "tests": [
